NickelKoSync
============

Keeps your reading position in sync with KOReader's progress sync server, from
inside Kobo's own software. Works with books read in Kobalt and in Nickel's
reader, and talks to the same server and account as KOReader and CrossPoint.

Set-up
------
1. Copy config.sample.ini to config.ini in this folder.
2. Fill in url (leave the default for the official server), username and
   password. These are the same as in KOReader > Progress sync.
3. Keep document_id = binary if the same book files are on all your devices
   (the usual case); use filename if only the names match.
4. Eject the Kobo. The mod re-reads config.ini within seconds; nothing to
   reboot. log.txt reports "signed in to ..." on the first sync.

How it syncs
------------
- When you close a book (in Kobalt or in Nickel's reader) the mod pushes the
  position to the server. If the device is offline it asks Nickel to connect to
  Wi-Fi (see [wifi] in config.ini) and pushes as soon as it is online.
- Whenever it is online it also checks the server for the recently read books.
  A newer position from another device is applied so the book opens there next
  time, in Kobalt and in Nickel's reader alike. If Kobalt has that very book
  open, Kobalt itself offers to move there (its usual message for a position
  changed elsewhere).
- A full check of the library (so a book begun on another device opens at
  the right place the first time here) runs at start, after Nickel's own Sync
  and on request: the "KOSync now" NickelMenu entry, which the mod adds by
  itself when NickelMenu is installed (menu / menu_log in config.ini), or an
  empty file named sync-now in this folder.
- A book that has only been opened here, at the cover, never overrides what
  another device stored for it.

Files in this folder
--------------------
config.ini          your settings (config.sample.ini is the reference)
state.json          the mod's memory: device id, what was pushed and applied
log.txt             what happened, newest at the end (log.txt.1 is older)
sync-now            create this empty file to trigger a sync
uninstall           create this empty file and reboot to remove the mod
                    (also delete .adds/nm/kosync if NickelMenu is installed)

Notes
-----
- Positions exchanged with KOReader and CrossPoint are exact to the paragraph
  and character for books read in Kobalt. For Nickel's reader they are exact
  to the kepub span (a sentence or so) for kepub files, and approximate for
  plain EPUB files.
- Only sideloaded books are synced (files on the Kobo's storage). Books from
  the Kobo store are not.
- Kobo's own cloud sync is not touched.
